# Public repo

Every commit is visible to the world. Never commit:

- Secrets: API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, `.pem`/`.p12`, SSH keys
- `.env*`, credentials JSON, service-account files
- Private personal data: home address, phone, exact DOB, ID numbers
- Internal work docs, private URLs with auth, or contact details the
  owner has not approved as public

Use placeholders (`hello@example.com`, `YOUR_TOKEN`). Keep build and
deploy secrets in Cloudflare Workers Builds or Cursor environment
secrets. Redact secrets in chat replies; never store the owner's
passwords or PATs in repo files.

If a secret may already be in git history, stop and warn the owner.
Rotation is required — deleting the file is not enough.

When unsure whether content should be public, ask first.
